  "t0001": "Mossstone Vestibule",
  "t0002": "Dripping Hall",
  "t0003": "Web Gallery",
  "t0004": "Wolfbone Pit",
  "t0005": "Lightless Channel",
  "t0006": "Ash Shrine",
  "t0007": "Statue Court",
  "t0008": "Wraith Well",
  "t0009": "Scorched Stair",
  "t0010": "The Ember Throne",
  "t0011": "Damp stone steps lead down. You light your lamp.",
  "t0012": "Water drips somewhere far off, like someone counting.",
  "t0013": "Fine threads hang in the air. They glint where your light touches them.",
  "t0014": "Gnawed bones litter the floor. Some of them are fresh.",
  "t0015": "The dark is thick here. Your light seems to drain away into it.",
  "t0016": "Ash covers the floor. Priests murmur behind the walls.",
  "t0017": "Every statue faces the way you came.",
  "t0018": "Weeping rises from the bottom of the well. The walls cannot keep it out.",
  "t0019": "Heat rolls up from the foot of the stair. Your wick crackles.",
  "t0020": "The fire before the throne has never gone out. The Ember King is waiting.",
  "t0021": "A hundred years ago, the heart of the Ember Lamp sank into the lamp well. The lamp-keeper who went down after it never came back. Since that day, the sky over the Lamp City has been black. The workshop has kept the Ember Lamp barely alight with the embers that delver after delver carried back up, but the flame shrinks every year, and it cannot last much longer. The old man at the workshop puts a small lamp in your hands. “The heart goes where it's warm. Follow the cold, and you're going down.” You step into the lamp well.",
  "t0022": "Day one. When the lamp's heart sank into the well, I was the only one who saw. I am this generation's lamp-keeper. My name is Liao. I will bring it back.",
  "t0023": "The water keeps counting. So do I: oil enough for four days. Count wrong, and there is no fifth.",
  "t0024": "Old lanterns hang along the webs, one after another. So the heart has sunk before, and others came down to look for it. Their lamps are all still here. Where are they?",
  "t0025": "Wolves don't fear the dark. What they fear is the silence just before a lamp goes out. I've learned to strike before it comes.",
  "t0026": "My lamp went out once. Something in the dark was biting me, and still I didn't feel cold at all. The heart is further down. I can feel its warmth.",
  "t0027": "The priests say the heart didn't fall. It wanted to come back, to the fire that first lit it. They say whoever stays to keep it company will never be cold again.",
  "t0028": "The statues all face the way I came, and every one holds a lamp. I counted to the twelfth, and didn't dare count further.",
  "t0029": "I've found the heart. It's so warm. I can't bear to let go. As long as I hold it, I never have to fear the dark again…",
  "t0030": "I'm not going back. The city can light another lamp. This fire is mine. (The rest of the page is scorched and curled.)",
