  "t0422": "<p class=\"muted\">You bring back <b style=\"color:var(--ember)\">{0}</b> embers{1} (total {2}). Trade them for permanent upgrades at the Lamp City Workshop on the title screen.</p>",
  "t0423": " (incl. {1} for the first Hard clear as {0})",
  "t0424": "<div class=\"stats\"><div><small>Depth</small><strong>{0}</strong></div><div><small>Level</small><strong>{1}</strong></div><div><small>Kills</small><strong>{2}</strong></div><div><small>Turns</small><strong>{3}</strong></div><div><small>Gold</small><strong>{4}</strong></div><div><small>Score</small><strong>{5}</strong></div></div>",
  "t0427": "The Ember King barely lifts a hand, and the fire before the throne surges toward you. Your lamp sways in the sea of flame and dims, until only a stubborn red point is left deep in the wick.",
  "t0428": "The Light Eater wants even your last glimmer. But a single spark slips out between its teeth.",
  "t0429": "Your oil is gone. The things in the dark finally close in, but they cannot reach that last red point deep in the wick.",
  "t0430": "The fire swallows you, but not your lamp. In the ashes, the wick still glows.",
  "t0431": "As you fall, the lamp rolls from your hand. The flame wavers a few times and dims. Only deep in the wick, a red point refuses to go out.",
  "t0432": "The depths fall quiet again. Your lamp lies on the stone, a stubborn red point still in its wick.",
  "t0433": "You could go no further. The flame in the wick shrinks and shrinks, down to a red point no bigger than a needle's tip, and still it will not go out.",
  "t0434": "That ember drifts up the lamp well, all the way back to the Lamp City. The old man at the workshop feeds it to the Ember Lamp, and the failing flame holds out one more night. “Another one's come back,” he says. The next to carry a lamp will take the city's hope down again.",
  "t0435": "A stone will rise where you fell. Next time you reach Floor {0}, you may find something there.",
  "t0436": "<h2>The Lamp Goes Out</h2><p>The {0} ({1}) {4} on Floor {2}, {3}.</p>{5}{6}{7}<p class=\"muted\">{8}{9}</p><div class=\"row\"><button class=\"btn hot\" id=\"mNew\">Same class</button><button class=\"btn\" id=\"mCls\">New class</button><button class=\"btn\" id=\"mTitle\">Title</button></div>",
  "t0437": "New high score! ",
  "t0438": "Daily Challenge ",
  "t0439": "Descend again",
  "t0440": "<h2>The Ember Lamp Rekindled{0}</h2><p>You hold the Emberheart and feel how warm it is, and you understand why Liao could not let go. But you turn anyway, and climb.</p><p>The {1} sets the Emberheart back in the lamp's cradle. Fire runs down the lamp well to the roots of the earth, then surges up into the sky. For the first time in a hundred years, the sky over the Lamp City grows light.</p>{2}{3}{4}<p class=\"muted\">{5}{6}</p><div class=\"row\"><button class=\"btn hot\" id=\"mNew\">Descend again</button><button class=\"btn\" id=\"mTitle\">Title</button></div>",
  "t0441": " · Hard",
  "t0442": "<div class=\"story\"><p>You did not leave Liao before the throne. You carried up the old lamp with his name on it too, and hung it beside the Ember Lamp.</p><p>The old man at the workshop looked at that lamp for a long time. Then he turned the register of those who went down to the page from a hundred years ago, struck out “Not returned” beside Liao's name, and wrote “Returned.”</p></div>{0}",
  "t0443": "<p class=\"muted\">First Hard clear as {0}: the class screen now bears the 燼 mark. Hard clears: {1} / 8 classes.</p>",
  "t0444": "The {0} takes up the lamp and enters the Emberlamp Abyss. Recover the Emberheart from Floor 10.",
