  "ui_cls_new": "New class unlocked: {0}",
  "cs_berserk_in": "You went down once before. Five of you went down; only you came back up. This time you carry no potions. Last time, it was the fight over the last one that split you apart.",
  "cs_berserk_end": "You did not turn back on Floor 9. On the night the sky grew light, you sat outside the workshop until dawn, and you did not dream of wolves. Beneath the lamp's cradle you carved four names, deep, so deep that another hundred years will not wear them away.",
  "cs_berserk_o1": "Faded headscarf",
  "cs_berserk_m1": "A-Dai's headscarf still hangs in the webs. That year he walked in front, and he was the first to see the old lanterns. He reached out to take one. You shouted at him not to touch it. The spiders were faster than your voice.",
  "cs_berserk_o2": "Half a torch",
  "cs_berserk_m2": "This is where the quarrel started: who should get the last Potion of Healing. That was when the torch fell. You remember that in the end, you were the one who took the potion. But however hard you try, you can't remember how you got it.",
  "cs_berserk_o3": "Notch in the wall",
  "cs_berserk_m3": "The sign you all agreed on is on the wall: whoever made it this far would carve a notch. There is only one notch. It's yours. Last time, this is where you turned back.",
  "cs_shadow_in": "You are the best thief in the Lamp City; on the south side they call you Sister Shade. You have stolen the workshop's oil, the altar's silver, the council's seal. This time someone has offered a price you can't refuse, for the Emberheart. You didn't ask who the buyer was.",
  "cs_shadow_end": "You did not hand the Emberheart to the buyer. You set it back in the lamp's cradle, and then, in the crowd packing the square, you found the one who had made the offer. His face looked far uglier in the light than it had in the dark. It was the first time in your life you gave back something already in your hands.",
  "cs_shadow_o1": "Old seal",
  "cs_shadow_m1": "A council seal lies on the ground, even older than the one you stole. So you weren't the only one ever to take this kind of job.",
  "cs_shadow_o2": "Empty purse",
  "cs_shadow_m2": "A purse lies buried in the ash, stitched with the sign the south-side thieves use to know their own, the same as the one inside your cuff. The purse is empty. He never got paid, and he never went back.",
  "cs_shadow_o3": "Note in the stones",
  "cs_shadow_m3": "A note is wedged in a crack in the stone, written in a hurry: “The buyer doesn't want the heart. He wants the Lamp City to stay dark.” You fold the note and tuck it into your innermost pocket.",
  "cs_monk_in": "In the lamp temple burns a row of vigil lamps, one for each person who never came back. There are more lamps every year, and the temple grows more crowded. You have decided to go down. Even if you can't bring them back, you will bring back their names.",
  "cs_monk_end": "You brought back more than a hundred names. That night, the lamp temple put out its vigil lamps one by one. Not because they were forgotten, but because they had finally come home. Only one lamp was left burning, and you would not say who it was for.",
  "cs_monk_o1": "Names on the lanterns",
  "cs_monk_m1": "Beneath each old lantern in the webs, a name is carved. You read them one by one. Several of those names have lamps burning in the temple. You chant a sutra for them. In the dark, the spiders go still.",
  "cs_monk_o2": "Blackened prayer beads",
  "cs_monk_m2": "The ash priest's prayer beads are just like the ones in your hand, except every bead is burned black. So they, too, once belonged to the lamp temple. You don't know on what day they began to pray to the fire instead of for people.",
  "cs_monk_o3": "Bronze bell by the well",
  "cs_monk_m3": "A bronze bell hangs over the Scorched Stair, cast in the same furnace as the temple's evening bell. You ring it. The weeping stops for a moment, as if everyone is counting: how much longer until their own name is called.",
  "cs_lamp_in": "You are the only apprentice of the old man at the workshop. His eyes can no longer make out a lamp's flame, yet every day he still polishes that small lamp. Today he puts the lamp in your hands and says nothing.",
  "cs_lamp_end": "You gave the lamp back to your master. He ran his fingers over the fresh scorch marks on its shade, and was silent a long time before he spoke. “I made it to Floor 9, and turned back. All these years, I thought it was my fault the Lamp City stayed dark.” You said, “You came back. That's why there was someone to teach me how to go on down.”",
  "cs_lamp_o1": "Mark on the wall",
  "cs_lamp_m1": "A workshop mark is carved into the wall, cut exactly the way your master taught you, only much older. You never knew he had come down here too.",
  "cs_lamp_o2": "Broken lamp hook",
  "cs_lamp_m2": "A lamp hook lies broken in the ash, its handle wrapped in the workshop's red cord. Your master's lamp hook has red cord on its handle too. Only his is new.",
  "cs_lamp_o3": "The last mark",
  "cs_lamp_m3": "The marks stop here. Beside them, in smaller strokes, someone has carved: “I'm sorry.” You remember now: on this day every year, your master keeps the workshop closed.",
  "cs_blade_in": "For seven years you guarded the mouth of the lamp well, charged with letting no one go down. In seven years you turned back over a hundred people. Only one slipped past you: your younger brother.",
  "cs_blade_end": "You planted your brother's broken sword at the mouth of the lamp well, right where you had stood for seven years. From that day on, no one stood guard there to stop people going down. Someone only waited there, for them to come back up.",
  "cs_blade_o1": "Red sword tassel",
  "cs_blade_m1": "A strand of red sword tassel is tangled in the spider silk. It was your gift to him when he came of age. You tied the knot yourself.",
  "cs_blade_o2": "Words written with a sword tip",
  "cs_blade_m2": "A few words are scratched into the ash with the tip of a sword: “Brother, I made it this far.” The strokes are neat, like when he practiced writing in the sand tray as a boy.",
  "cs_blade_o3": "Broken sword",
  "cs_blade_m3": "His sword lies broken on the stair, point down, as if showing you the way. You did not find him. You strap the broken sword to your back and keep going down.",
  "cs_rune_in": "In the archives you read every book about the lamp well, and found something no one had noticed: this is not the first time the heart has sunk. Every hundred years, it sinks again.",
  "cs_rune_end": "You wrote everything you saw on the way down into a book, and set it in the most prominent place in the archives. On the cover is a single line: “Next time, don't wait until dark.”",
  "cs_rune_o1": "Three sets of lanterns",
  "cs_rune_m1": "You count the lanterns in the webs and sort them by style into three sets. The oldest set matches the designs from three hundred years ago in the archives exactly. Each set is one sinking.",
  "cs_rune_o2": "List on the wall",
  "cs_rune_m2": "You can read half the runes on the shrine wall. They are not a spell. They are a list: after each sinking, the people who stayed below to keep the heart company. The newest line is buried under ash.",
  "cs_rune_o3": "The finished reckoning",
  "cs_rune_m3": "On the stair, you finish the reckoning. Each time the heart sank, it was after the last person in the city who remembered the sinking before had died.",
