  "ui_city_title": "Lamp City Workshop",
  "ui_city_intro": "For the first time in a hundred years the Lamp City has light, but many streets are still dark. Send the embers you bring back into the city and light it, one district at a time.",
  "ui_city_have": "You have <b style=\"color:var(--ember)\">{0}</b> embers.",
  "ui_city_dark": "Still dark.",
  "ui_city_locked": "Light the previous district first.",
  "ui_city_read": "Revisit",
  "ui_city_all": "The Lamp City is fully lit. Every lamp is someone who came home.",
  "city_workshop": "Workshop Street",
  "city_workshop_s": "The lamps of Workshop Street come on one by one. The old man stands in the workshop doorway for a long time and, for once, doesn’t cough. “This street used to be this bright,” he says.",
  "city_temple": "Lamp Temple",
  "city_temple_s": "The temple’s evening bell rings again. A young novice counts every stroke, and at the hundred and eighth, no one in the temple is weeping.",
  "city_shrine": "Lamp Shrine",
  "city_shrine_s": "The shrine’s lamps bloom, and this time the flowers face upward. The eldest maiden says it is the first true good omen in a hundred years.",
  "city_south": "South Lanes",
  "city_south_s": "The south lanes are lit, and the thieves aren’t used to it. Someone sneaks a stolen lamp back where it belongs in the night, muttering: too bright, nowhere to hide.",
  "city_archive": "Archive",
  "city_archive_s": "The archive’s lamps burn until dawn. The copyist closes the volume on the sinkings, opens a new one and writes on the first page: dawn has come.",
  "city_smithy": "Smithy",
  "city_smithy_s": "The smithy lights its forge again. The smith opens the old ledger, strikes a line through “Old Qin, three coppers,” and tells his apprentice: no need to pay.",
  "city_gate": "Well-mouth Post",
  "city_gate_s": "The guard post at the mouth of the well stands empty. No one keeps people from going down anymore; a lamp hangs at its door, waiting for people to come up.",
  "city_ferry": "Ferrier’s Shop",
  "city_ferry_s": "The ferrier’s shop stands open, name tags and red string laid out neatly on the table. Fewer people come now: there are fewer lamps that need carrying home.",
  "city_square": "Well Square",
  "city_square_s": "Well Square is the last to light. People hang the old lamps they brought back in a ring, and someone starts an old, old song. The song of the Lamp City — some say they heard it once, deep down the well.",
  "ui_full_cls_lock": "A full-version class. Even with the full version, clear the game as the {0} first to unlock it. Tap to learn more",
  "ui_gal_t5": "Lamp City",
  "ui_gal_lock5": "Light<br>{0}",
  "ui_gal_cityall": "Lamp City · Group Picture",
  "ui_gal_lockall": "Light all nine districts of Lamp City",
  "ui_city_more": "Continue",
  "lw_title": "Liao",
  "lw_cold": "He looks at the lamp in your hand and says, very softly, “…So cold.”",
  "lw_end": "Then his fingers open. A heart of fire, still beating, drops to the ground.",
  "lw_a": "Bring your lamp close to him.",
  "lw_a_r": "He squints at it for a long time. “…So a lamp is warm. I held this fire for a hundred years, and it was never as warm as this.”",
  "lw_b": "Take his hand. Say nothing.",
  "lw_b_r": "His hand is cold, but he smiles. “…So you don’t have to hold the fire to stop being cold.”",
  "lw_blade": "“I guarded the well for seven years. No one was to go down. …My brother went down anyway.”",
  "lw_blade_r": "“…If only someone had stopped me, back then.” He looks at the broken sword on your back. “Go home. Stop guarding the well against the ones going down. Wait there for the ones coming up.”",
  "lw_lamp": "Light the old lamp that went out a hundred years ago.",
  "lw_lamp_r": "When the old lamp catches, he watches it for a long time. “…So bright. All this time, I was waiting for someone to light it for me.”",
  "lw_miko": "“The shrine’s lamp bloomed, its flower facing down. So it was you, keeping a lamp lit down here all this time.”",
  "lw_miko_r": "“…I thought no one could see it.” He smiles faintly. “When you go back up, the flower will face upward.”",
  "lw_monk": "“Among the everlasting lamps in the temple, one bears your name.”",
  "lw_monk_r": "“…Still lit, after a hundred years?” He is silent a long while. “Let it go out. I’m going home.”",
  "lw_shadow": "“Someone’s paying a fortune for that fire in your hands. …But I’m not selling.”",
  "lw_shadow_r": "“…A thief?” To your surprise, he laughs. “Then you’re better than me. I stole a whole city’s light and could never bring myself to give it back.”",
  "lw_rune": "“The heart sinks once every hundred years. This time, I’ll make the city remember.”",
  "lw_rune_r": "“…Remembering is enough.” He looks at the old lamp at his waist. “Then write me in. Write how I came to stay, so the next one won’t do as I did.”",
  "lw_berserk": "“I carry something I can’t put down, too. Four names.”",
  "lw_berserk_r": "“…What I couldn’t let go of was a fire, so I couldn’t go back.” He looks at you, as if something has eased. “What you can’t let go of are names. You’ll make it back.”",
  "lw_ferry": "“I’m a lamp ferrier. I’ll take you home.”",
  "lw_ferry_r": "“…Then I’m in your hands.” He closes his eyes. “This time, I’ll follow you.”",
  "ui_bk": "Back up records",
